Notebook[{Cell["ImportGroupData", "ObjectName"], 
  Cell["ImportGroupData[file, opts] reads a mathematical snapshot into a \
fresh Group after independent registered-export or actual native \
correspondence validation.", "Usage"], Cell["Status: Alpha.", "Notes"], 
  Cell["Returns a fresh live Group with saved mathematical IDs/orderings. \
Every file passes schema checks. Matching independent locally registered \
bytes (the user's own export ledger or the package's library ledger) import \
without GAP, even after workspace eviction, and without re-checking their \
mathematics: they were verified when saved, so they are decoded once and \
their character table and CG coefficients are not re-proved. Verification -> \
\"Exact\" re-checks a registered file like an unknown one.", "Notes"], 
  Cell["Unknown typed snapshots are verified against an independently \
constructed actual group, complete characters and optional data. \
ValidationGroup instead supplies accepted source state and never waives \
correspondence checks; the supplied object is unchanged.", "Notes"], 
  Cell["Unregistered raw-code snapshots require ValidationGroup built \
explicitly from the same recipe and generator order. Neither imported code \
nor imported workspace paths are executed. Unsupported schema, changed files \
or false claims return Failure.", "Notes"], Cell["Known mathematical \
identities retain their accepted bindings, including after a restart through \
the independent export ledger. Reassigning character/class, generator, \
modular-assignment, subgroup or subgroup-class IDs returns Failure. \
Consistent row/class reorderings remain valid.", "Notes"], 
  Cell["GroupModel affects character-source construction for an unknown typed \
snapshot with ValidationGroup->Automatic. Registered imports and an explicit \
ValidationGroup reuse accepted data; the final correspondence checks use the \
original recorded group.", "Notes"], Cell["Moving a large computation between \
machines: run BuildGroup and SaveGroupData where the resources are, copy the \
snapshot, and call ImportGroupData locally. A typed snapshot unknown to the \
local ledger is checked by rebuilding only the actual group and its \
characters in the local GAP. The saved representations are verified against \
them, never recomputed. A raw GAP result produced without the package cannot \
be imported, because it carries no checkable provenance.", "Notes"], 
  Cell["Saved CG coefficients:\n- In a registered snapshot (the package's own \
unchanged export or a library file, with no ValidationGroup and Verification \
not \"Exact\"), only their identities and keys are checked on import; each \
keeps its recorded status and is served without a check (an \"Unverified\" \
entry is checked on its first use at a verifying level, a \"Numerical\" one \
when a call asks for \"Exact\").\n- In any other file imported at Automatic \
or \"Exact\", every saved bundle is validated exactly on import; at \
\"Numerical\" or None the bundles are kept \"Unverified\" and are checked on \
their first use at a verifying level.", "Notes"], 
  Cell["Options (shared configured settings can override these defaults):", 
   "Notes"], Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{{Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["GroupModel"], "TableText"], Cell["Automatic", 
        "TableText"], Cell["Automatic, \"Original\", \"Permutation\" or \
\"PC\" for new method calculations; PC requires a solvable group. Restoration \
and compatible cache hits do not convert models. Import uses it only when \
computing a new character-validation source.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["StoreGAPState"], 
        "TableText"], Cell["True", "TableText"], Cell["True retains verified \
state across calls; False keeps only call-local temporary checkpoints. Cached \
mathematical values remain available.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["AttemptTimeLimit"], 
        "TableText"], Cell["600", "TableText"], Cell["Positive seconds or \
Infinity, per attempt including verification and saving. Automatic method \
attempts each receive this limit.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["CoreBudget"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], Cell["Positive integer at most \
$ProcessorCount, or Automatic to use the available count. Sequential \
algorithms run as separate worker processes.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["MemoryBudget"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], Cell["Positive integer bytes, or \
Automatic using half system memory less current kernel usage. Admission \
estimates and sampled total worker RSS enforce the allocation.", 
        "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["ProgressFunction"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], Cell["Automatic shows a notebook \
monitor when a front end is available; None is silent; a Function or user \
symbol receives progress associations. Callbacks should return promptly; \
failures/cancellation clean owned workers.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["ValidationGroup"], 
        "TableText"], Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], 
       Cell["Automatic or a live accepted Group. Explicit validation is \
honored even for locally registered snapshots. Unknown raw snapshots require \
an explicit matching source.", "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["Verification"], "TableText"], Cell["Automatic", 
        "TableText"], Cell["Automatic, \"Exact\", \"Numerical\" or None (the \
Validate functions: Automatic, \"Exact\" or \"Numerical\"; the modular-form \
functions have no \"Exact\" route).", "TableText"]}}, 
     GridBoxAlignment -> {"Columns" -> {{Left}}}, GridBoxItemSize -> 
      {"Columns" -> {Scaled[0.02], Scaled[0.3], Scaled[0.18], 
         Scaled[0.5]}}]], "3ColumnTableMod"], 
  Cell["See Also", "SeeAlsoSection"], 
  Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["SaveGroupData", BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", 
      ButtonData -> {"SaveGroupData.nb", None}], "  |  ", 
     ButtonBox["RestoreGAPState", BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", 
      ButtonData -> {"RestoreGAPState.nb", None}], "  |  ", 
     ButtonBox["ValidationGroup", BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", 
      ButtonData -> {"ValidationGroup.nb", None}]}], "SeeAlso"], 
  Cell["Examples Initialization", "ExamplesInitializationSection"], 
  Cell["Open this notebook in its repository location. GAP must be installed; \
LINS is required for its bounded search page. Evaluate the setup before the \
examples.", "ExampleText"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{RowBox[{"Get", "[", RowBox[{"FileNameJoin", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"Nest", "[", RowBox[{"DirectoryName", 
                  ",", RowBox[{"NotebookFileName", "[", "]"}], ",", "5"}], 
                "]"}], ",", "\"Kernel\"", ",", "\"init.m\""}], "}"}], "]"}], 
        "]"}], ";"}]], "ExampleInitialization"], 
  Cell["Basic Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
      RowBox[{RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"g", "=", RowBox[{"BuildGroup", 
                "[", RowBox[{RowBox[{"CatalogueGroup", "[", RowBox[
                     {"\"CyclicGroup\"", ",", "3"}], "]"}], ",", 
                  RowBox[{"ComputeRepresentations", "\[Rule]", "False"}], 
                  ",", RowBox[{"StoreGAPState", "\[Rule]", "False"}]}], 
                "]"}]}], ",", RowBox[{"d", "=", RowBox[{"CreateDirectory", 
                "[", "]"}]}], ",", "p", ",", "h"}], "}"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"WithCleanup", "[", RowBox[{"Null", ",", 
            RowBox[{RowBox[{"p", "=", RowBox[{"SaveGroupData", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"g", ",", RowBox[{"FileNameJoin", "[", RowBox[
                       {"{", RowBox[{"d", ",", "\"group.json\""}], "}"}], 
                      "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", RowBox[{"h", "=", 
                RowBox[{"ImportGroupData", "[", RowBox[{"p", ",", RowBox[
                     {"StoreGAPState", "\[Rule]", "False"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", 
              RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"h", "=!=", "g"}], ",", 
                  RowBox[{RowBox[{"h", "[", "\"CharacterData\"", "]"}], 
                    "===", RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"CharacterData\"", "]"}]}]}], 
                "}"}]}], ",", RowBox[{"DeleteDirectory", "[", 
              RowBox[{"d", ",", RowBox[{"DeleteContents", "\[Rule]", 
                  "True"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input", 
   CellTags -> "VerifiedExample"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"True", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output"], 
  Cell["Possible Issues", "ExampleSection"], Cell["Invalid input returns a \
structured Failure. Check FailureQ before using the result.", "ExampleText"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"FailureQ", "[", RowBox[{"ImportGroupData", "[", 
        "\"\"", "]"}], "]"}]], "Input", CellTags -> "VerifiedErrorExample"], 
  Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output"], Cell["Related Guides", 
   "MoreAboutSection"], 
  Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["Constructing finite groups", 
      BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", ButtonData -> 
       {"../../Tutorials/ConstructingFiniteGroups.nb", None}]}], 
   "MoreAbout"], Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Metadata", "MetadataSection"], 
     Cell["Symbol", "Categorization", CellLabel -> "Entity Type"], 
     Cell["VVMFTool", "Categorization", CellLabel -> "Paclet Name"], 
     Cell["VVMFTool`", "Categorization", CellLabel -> "Context"], 
     Cell["VVMFTool/ref/ImportGroupData", "Categorization", 
      CellLabel -> "URI"]}, Closed]]}, 
 WindowTitle -> "ImportGroupData \[LongDash] VVMFTool", 
 WindowSize -> {1000, 850}, TaggingRules -> <|"Paclet" -> "VVMFTool", 
   "Status" -> "Alpha"|>, StyleDefinitions -> FrontEnd`FileName[{"Wolfram"}, 
